{"duration_api_ms":25309,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"015b3b85-9950-4db5-a933-d2839024c262","total_cost_usd":0.24447500000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21420,"cache_read_input_tokens":176315,"output_tokens":1891,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":137},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21420,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1288,"cache_read_input_tokens":48345,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5529},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":1891,"cacheReadInputTokens":176315,"cacheCreationInputTokens":21420,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24447500000000005,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":137,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":21420,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SC9uDjXfXeZ33rvdkTyT87","tool_input":{"command":"cd /home/claude/euro-office-server.theseus-worktrees/PKT-0109; f=$(grep -rl \"PKT-0109\" .theseus/queue | head -3); echo \"$f\"; cat $(echo \"$f\"|head -1); git diff --stat 095ea03898c2387cb0a5233bbfb058ccaef005f2..HEAD; git -C external/sdkjs diff --stat refs/theseus/base..HEAD","description":"Read packet and diff stats"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I approve PKT-0109. It's an investigate packet: it measures redraw cost rather than changing code, so the rule about rejecting a performance packet with no measured gain doesn't apply. The sdkjs fork has no commits on `pkt/PKT-0109`; the only changes are in this repository.\n\n**Goal coverage.**\n- **Script:** `word-repaint.js` sets up the test as asked. It injects the fork build through Playwright routing, as PKT-0093 does, and opens `large-100p.docx` as users A and B.\n- **What it wraps:** the CDocument and DrawingDocument redraw entry points, `OnRecalculatePage`, `UpdateTarget`, `CEditorPage.OnPaint` and `drawImage`.\n- **What it records:** per local keystroke and per remote change, it counts pages recalculated, pages redrawn, redraw calls, `drawImage` calls and time spent in each.\n- **Table and call sites:** both are in `baseline.md`, with file and approximate line references for the code that decides how much gets redrawn.\n- **Ceilings:**\n  - The `NOCLEAR` variant gives a measured upper bound for skipping the all-pages lock redraw in `Send_Changes`: re-rendered pages go from 1.8 to 1 per keystroke, and paint time from 30 to 18 ms.\n  - The ceiling for redrawing only the changed lines is an estimate, not a prototype, and it is labelled as one.\n\n**Things it leaves open, all stated openly.**\n- **\"Rectangles\" means pages here.** The executor logged this as a decision. sdkjs word only invalidates whole pages, so there is no smaller rectangle to count.\n- **Remote fast-path recalc is not timed.** The table's 0 ms remote p50 for recalculation therefore means \"not measured\", not \"no work\". `baseline.md` says so explicitly. This is a real gap, since the goal asked for ms for each step. I don't think it calls the findings into question: the largest remote cost, the full-document recalc fallback, is measured, and a follow-up packet is requested to trace why that fallback happens.\n- **Each side has only 2 runs × 20 events.** That's a small sample, but it is enough for an investigation, and it is reported as p50 and mean.\n\n**Method checks.**\n- The Executor log is filled in.\n- The `Spawned packets` section lists both follow-ups, and both request files are in `.theseus/spawn/`.\n- The friction line is appended to `.theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl`.\n- 6 files changed against a budget of 6. 406 lines added against a budget of 800.\n- Nothing in `contract.preserve` was touched: no tests or source code changed.\n\n**The retry.** The earlier rejection was a single unexplained difference from `differential/sdkjs-word.sh`. It can't come from this packet, because the fork is unchanged (`theseus` 0f61ccc, the same build as the base). The executor re-ran it twice and it passed both times. The differential output supplied with this review compares the same build on both sides and also reports all checks the same. The executor's suggestion is worth taking up for the method: the oracle should keep the name of the check that differed and re-run a differing check once before failing a packet.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE measurements, call sites and ceilings recorded as asked; gaps (remote fast-path recalc not timed, line-level ceiling estimated) are stated and follow-ups requested","ttft_ms":5510,"type":"result","duration_ms":25814,"uuid":"3dc33de8-5530-4a55-acd6-3aad688600a9","ttft_stream_ms":3623,"time_to_request_ms":345,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":270,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":4,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":2,"auto_mode_context_wait":5,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":4},